        "v": 5,
        "title": "npm-app package refactor with compiled binary release workflow",
        "summary": "Monorepo restructured: `common` package renamed `@codebuff/common`, `backend` scoped to `@codebuff/backend` with ESM (`\"type\": \"module\"`), and `npm-app` extracted as standalone buildable package. New `release-binaries.yml` workflow compiles Bun binaries via `npm-app/scripts/build-binary.js`, with `patch-bun-pty.ts` and `patch-web-tree-sitter.ts` patching native deps for static compilation. CI split into separate web build, typecheck, and npm-app build steps; `.manicodeignore` replaced by `.codebuffignore`. Jest config drops `@/env` module mapper in favor of direct relative imports.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T13:09:33.830Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The software project has been reorganized so that its different parts can be built and packaged more reliably for distributing pre-compiled programs. Previously bundled together components have been separated into distinct, clearly named packages, and a new automated process now compiles standalone executable programs from the code. If you were to look at the project today, the build process runs separately for the web interface, type checking, and the main application package, and certain internal configuration and dependency setups have been adjusted for this new structure.",
